WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Mifune

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Touto

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.160
<i>It's the prelims of the Regionals,</i>

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.320
<i>and the score is tied going 
into the bottom of the third.</i>

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.480
All Satou's doing to change 
the direction of his pitches

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.030
Touto Boys

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.030
First base  Mayumura Michiru

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.290
is stepping on different 
parts of the rubber.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.530
Pitcher

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.530
Satou Hikaru

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.690
No matter how fast the pitch is, 
if we know where the ball's going,

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.370
we've basically defanged him.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.540
<i>Are you kidding me?</i>

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.220
<i>The secret to his newfound control
is something so simple?</i>

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.790
<i>Hikaru's been pitching very well up to now.</i>

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:37.170
<i>But the Touto Boys' Mayumura siblings 
are a real force to be reckoned with.</i>

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.280
<i>Batting second, second base, Hirata-kun.</i>

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:21.120
Daigo and Hikaru

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.580
No outs and a runner on second!

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.640
Hirata, keep us rolling!

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:29.070
<i>It's okay. Even if they know where 
the ball's going, with Hikaru's power,</i>

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:31.630
<i>it still won't be easy to 
get a hit off his pitches.</i>

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.090
<i>Outside.</i>

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:39.880
Out!

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.260
<i>Outside.</i>

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:48.930
Nice running!

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.880
<i>A tag up. They're leaving no stone unturned.</i>

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.110
<i>We've got two outs, but...</i>

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.070
Touto Boys

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.070
Catcher  Mayumura Wataru

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.980
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, 
Mayumura Wataru-kun</i>

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.320
<i>This batter won't let us 
off the hook so easily.</i>

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.200
<i>Inside.</i>

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.330
Foul!

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.590
<i>He threw outside?</i>

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.090
<i>Guess he must've realized 
we'd figured him out.</i>

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.590
<i>But I won't miss again!</i>

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:26.680
Ball!

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.340
<i>He's trying to control the 
ball with his wrist action</i>

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.490
<i>so they can't just look at where 
his foot is on the rubber.</i>

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:35.560
Ball!

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:38.730
Ball!

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.950
Three balls. One strike.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:49.910
<i>If I can't fine-tune my aim, 
I'll just have to overpower them!</i>

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.150
Yeah!

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.750
You did it!

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.280
Awesome, Wataru!

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.160
He got us.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.850
That should make their shoulders drop.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.290
I think that one went about 100 meters.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.510
<i>Batting fifth, right field, Kouzaka-kun.</i>

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.510
Aw, man! They took the lead again.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.480
Mifune Dolphins

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.480
Coach  Fujii

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.480
Mifune Dolphins

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.480
Manager  Tashiro

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.480
Shake it off, Satou.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:04:59.020
What?

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.800
All right! Two homers in a row! 4-1!

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:10.620
<i>It's no use.</i>

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.370
<i>The Touto Boys are just too good.</i>

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.830
First base

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.830
Suzuki Andy

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.830
Three runs behind...

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.630
Left field

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.630
Urabe Hayato

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:19.630
Even if I took to the mound now, 
they'd just light me up.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.590
Shortstop

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.590
Kimura

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.590
Crud.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.900
<i>D-Damn it!</i>

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:26.650
Ball!

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.340
Ball!

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:29.890
Ball!

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.740
Ball four!

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.140
Time out!

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.960
Put those home runs out of your mind.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:43.150
That was the meat of Touto's order.
 There was nothing you could do.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:46.290
But we can't keep walking their batters.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.070
It's the bottom of their lineup 
now, so just let them swing.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.120
Manager.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.080
You can swap me out for Urabe-kun now.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.240
Huh?!

00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:01.640
I've tried a few things, but it looks like 
I don't have the weaponry to win this.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.200
I'm sorry I couldn't live up 
to your expectations.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:08.550
All right.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:11.670
But Urabe hasn't warmed up his arm yet.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.500
We only need one more out.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.560
Please see out this inning for us.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:16.270
All right.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.750
<i>Batting seventh, third base, Nakamura-kun.</i>

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:23.640
Play!

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.270
<i>I've never seen Hikaru 
looking so discouraged...</i>

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:33.120
Huh?

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:33.820
Hey!

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:34.910
There's a runner!

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.990
Run, Kotouge!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:39.460
Ball!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.170
Safe!

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:46.630
I forgot about the runner. My bad.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:52.030
Looks like that kid's concentration 
has gone out the window.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.120
Yeah.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:55.760
I think they want him to see out the inning.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:59.850
I just hope doing so doesn't 
further dent his confidence.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:04.610
He got it!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.570
What?!

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.510
Hikaru, cover first base!

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.240
Safe!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.430
Yeah! Awesome! Runners on first and third!

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.120
Hikaru!

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.460
Oh... sorry.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:26.670
<i>Come on, Hikaru.</i>

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:29.160
<i>Grit your teeth and bear it.</i>

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.520
<i>We can still make up a three-run deficit.</i>

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:36.610
<i>Huh?</i>

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.340
<i>What the...</i>

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:43.750
<i>Was baseball... always such a grind?</i>

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.020
He's running!

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:49.950
Hey!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.320
Balk!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:01.850
Sweet freebie!

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.120
5-1!

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.920
S-Sorry, I think I just got flustered.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:11.590
I'm disappointed.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.960
We couldn't do anything 
about those home runs.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:19.240
Forgetting to use the set because of 
those gut punches is understandable.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:22.430
But your errors after 
that weren't even errors!

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.620
You've just given up on the game!

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:28.880
Because your pitching 
isn't working against them,

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.860
you've stopped caring altogether!

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:35.360
You wouldn't be playing so absentmindedly 
if you still cared about this game.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.640
I don't want to lose like this.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:41.790
In fact, I still intend to win this game.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:00.250
Keep us rolling, Sakai! 
This is another chance!

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:09.820
You've just given up on the game!

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.240
I still intend to win this game.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:16.280
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:24.910
Daigo!

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.630
Out! Three outs! Change sides!

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.050
Nice one, Daigo!

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:34.580
Daigo-kun, are you okay?

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.080
I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.430
Nice pitching.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.310
Mifune

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.310
Touto

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:42.310
5-1, huh?

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:44.160
Not bad, I guess.

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:47.730
We're on track to get 
the game called in the fifth.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:53.610
Let's face it. I wildly underestimated Touto.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.940
We were relying on Satou, 
but if they can hit his pitches...

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.990
Urabe, start warming up your arm.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.010
You're pitching next inning.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:01.740
What?

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.350
Satou asked me to switch you in.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.950
Andy will be your catcher.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.830
So get yourselves warmed up.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.460
Y-Yessir.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.940
But Andy's batting first this inning.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:14.560
Oh, yeah, I am.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.870
I'll help you warm up while he's out there.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:19.060
Has your nose stopped bleeding?

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:21.430
It's fine. I stuffed some 
cotton balls up there.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.700
Manager.

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:29.060
I'm going to bow out now.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:34.250
From here on out, please let 
Nagai-kun field and bat in my place.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:35.030
What?

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.550
Hikaru-kun?!

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:41.310
<i>Bottom of the fourth, Dolphins to bat.</i>

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:44.000
<i>Batting fourth, first base, Suzuki-kun.</i>

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:47.580
Daigo-kun yelled at me earlier.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:50.870
He said I shouldn't play 
as if I've already given up.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.420
Strike!

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:57.370
That's when realization washed over me.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.180
Once I got hit and didn't look
so cool anymore, I stopped caring.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:06.930
I'm not obsessed with baseball. 
I don't have any passion for the game.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:13.670
If a newcomer like me can help the 
team win, then it's another matter.

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.900
But as I can't, I'm useless to you.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.650
Someone like me has no right being
on the field one second longer.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.120
Right field

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.120
Sakura Mutsuko

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:29.960
That's why I'd rather you played guys who've
 been on the team a lot longer than I have.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.960
Please let the <i>real</i> baseball lovers,

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:37.050
Nagai

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.370
who have trained so hard 
over the years, take to the field.

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:39.320
Foul.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:46.010
Here. Thanks for lending them to me, Nagai-kun.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.730
You absolute <i>moron</i>!

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.340
What the hell, man?!

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:59.890
"Please let Nagai bat in my place"?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.240
Third base

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.240
Ariyoshi

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:03.990
Screw you with your "let the real 
baseball lovers take to the field" spiel!

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.990
Matsubara

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.990
Center field

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.990
Kishimoto

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:05.590
Who do you think you are?!

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:08.290
You think doing this will make us happy?

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:12.530
Stop trying to look cool when all 
you're doing is running away, you idiot!

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.130
What's going on?

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.340
Safe! Safe!

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:28.390
That guy...

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:30.820
His leg hasn't even fully healed yet.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.590
Satou, nobody's subbing in for you just yet.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.540
This isn't the right time 
to remove our fifth batter.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.220
All right.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:45.860
Hey, Satou!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:51.470
Listen up! I only want to play when I can 
bask in the glory of causing an upset!

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:55.040
If you wanna swap out for me, you'd 
better set it up so I get that opportunity!

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:58.940
Besides, you can still claw 
this back with your bat!

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.550
Stop hiding how upset you really are!

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:03.560
Use your own two hands to 
take back what they took from you!

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.900
<i>Batting fifth, pitcher, Satou-kun.</i>

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:16.310
Play!

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:30.860
<i>This guy's giving off a weird vibe.</i>

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:33.220
<i>After him, it's their bottom order.</i>

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:35.370
<i>You don't have to face him head-on, Komatsu.</i>

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.830
Touto Boys

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.830
Pitcher  Komatsu

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:40.790
Strike!

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.300
Hey, now. What's he swinging at?

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:47.390
Stop hiding how upset you really are!

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:50.140
Use your own two hands to 
take back what they took from you!

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:53.390
Calm down, Satou!

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.440
Hey, over here!

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:03.650
Safe!

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:06.620
What does he think he's doing?

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:10.160
He's got an injured leg, and he was
never a base stealer, anyway!

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:15.160
Hey, hey!

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:17.780
Ball!

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:20.380
Safe!

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:21.420
Hey, And—

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.530
No, it's okay.

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:25.530
He's not trying to steal.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.820
He's trying to put some 
pressure on their pitcher.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:30.890
Huh?

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:34.650
Well, he saw Satou's first swing.

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:37.270
Andy's probably trying to buy 
him some time to calm down.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:39.170
I see.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.940
Hey, hey.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.160
Over here. Over here.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:46.630
<i>You're a butterball like me.</i>

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.150
<i>You think you can run?!</i>

00:14:50.270 --> 00:14:50.980
Safe!

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:52.240
Damn you!

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.020
Time out!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.380
What are you doing?!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.800
With our lead, we don't have 
to worry about the runner!

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:01.460
After him, it's their bottom order.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.880
You can even let Satou walk.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.380
Focus on the batter!

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.470
Besides, do you really think 
that guy could steal second?!

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.470
He's just toying with you!

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:16.870
<i>He's not a fast runner, 
and he's playing with an injury.</i>

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.660
<i>But he's still trying 
to rattle their battery.</i>

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:21.160
<i>Is he trying to assist me?</i>

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:22.790
<i>Is he doing this for me?</i>

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.860
You've just given up on the game!

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.360
Stop trying to look cool when all 
you're doing is running away!

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:32.210
Strike two!

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:34.740
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:36.660
<i>It's not for me.</i>

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:41.650
<i>Everybody's giving it their 
all in order to win this game!</i>

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.800
<i>I was a fool!</i>

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:54.360
<i>Of </i>course<i> pitching and hitting 
is fun when you're winning!</i>

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:59.980
<i>But in the end, whether it's going 
well or badly... baseball is...</i>

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:07.290
<i>Baseball is fun because 
everyone's giving it all they've got!</i>

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.970
It's gone!

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:35.530
That was amazing!

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:37.460
It's 5-3 now. We can turn this around!

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:39.120
You've restored my faith, man!

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:40.110
No.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:46.300
It was you and the rest of 
the team who restored mine.

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:55.730
<i>That Satou Hikaru is bad news.</i>

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:59.870
<i>I've never seen anyone hit an outside
pitch farther than Wataru before.</i>

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.200
Strike! Batter out!

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.210
Mifune

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.210
Touto

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:05.450
Three outs! Change sides!

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:08.500
Urabe's going to pitch now.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:09.920
Andy will play catcher.

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:12.910
Satou, you'll switch with 
Kishimoto in center field.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:16.620
Daigo, you're out in left field. Be ready to 
jump in if Andy's injury flares up again.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:18.440
Matsubara, you're on first base.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:19.770
That's all.

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:20.680
Yes, sir!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.320
Huh?

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:25.480
They've changed their battery.

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.930
Satou was ineffective, 
so they're putting in Urabe?

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:33.680
Even though we figured him out, 
Satou's fastballs were more of a nuisance.

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:35.320
Looks like we got a lucky break.

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:40.070
Against Urabe, we can get twice 
as many runs as they did last inning.

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:43.890
Nice, Urabe. Your pitches
are really flying today.

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:45.500
Huh? You think so?

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.250
Yeah, I mean it.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:49.880
Anyway, just throw to where I signal.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.510
Looks like that's all we can do.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:00.270
<i>Bottom of the fourth, Touto Boys to bat.</i>

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:03.260
<i>Batting ninth, pitcher, Komatsu-kun.</i>

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:05.890
Okay, we just need two runs. Two runs!

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:07.450
Yeah, Urabe! You can do it!

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:10.860
<i>I know!</i>

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.360
<i>This day...</i>

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:15.610
<i>This moment...</i>

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.240
<i>...is the reason we've been doing all of this!</i>

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:23.620
Strike! Out!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:24.480
Yes!

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:26.120
Nice pitching, Urabe!

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:29.960
<i>Batting first, first base, 
Mayumura Michiru-san.</i>

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:33.590
Strike!

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:36.360
That kid's not bad, either.

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:37.470
Yeah.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.530
He's coming in on the low side,

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:42.360
and he's throwing the ball
directly into the catcher's mitt.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.140
Foul!

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:49.270
Ball!

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:52.970
That one was just for show.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:56.300
The catcher's using his head 
and calling an excellent game.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.440
His speed might only be average,

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:01.660
but if the pitcher keeps throwing 
with that level of control,

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:04.220
he'll cause issues for 
even the best batters.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:10.320
Batter out!

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:15.500
Urabe-kun, nice pitching!

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:18.880
<i>So </i>that's<i> what pitching is about.</i>

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:21.620
<i>Pitchers are more than
 just their fastballs.</i>

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.710
What happened, Michiru? 
Even you're struggling?

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:28.980
A pitcher like that shouldn't 
be striking you out!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.120
You're slacking!

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:34.070
That outside ball was just for show.

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:36.860
The rest were all inside.

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:37.910
What?

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:40.240
So he was throwing to your weaker side?

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:41.730
Exactly.

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:44.650
Strike! Batter out!

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.300
All right!

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:47.620
Nice one, Urabe! Well done!

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:48.700
Tch.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:51.790
I think you're the one who's slacking, Wataru.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:52.850
What?!

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:56.190
You should stop underestimating 
Urabe and Andy.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.260
We were distracted by Satou and Shigeno,

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.590
but it's those two who 
are Mifune's backbone.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.510
Mifune

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.510
Touto

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:09.770
Oh, 5-3, huh? They're putting up a good fight.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.250
Izumi! Practice over already?

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:13.250
Yup.

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:16.400
I really thought they would've 
called the game by now.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:18.660
Is Daigo doing okay?

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:20.490
He's doing great!

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.960
He got a bunt and a squeeze, 
so that's one base hit and one RBI!

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:25.620
Oh, not bad!

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:28.580
All right!

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:30.450
Sakura got another hit!

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:34.920
Okay! We've got to get some more runners 
on base, and then, convert somehow.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.920
<i>Batting first, shortstop, Kimura-kun.</i>

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:37.920
<i>Who is that Number 9?</i>

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:41.550
<i>The pitch wasn't bad, but she got another hit!</i>

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:44.400
<i>Anyway, we can't let them score any more runs!</i>

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.280
First!

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:49.930
Out!

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:52.930
Nice bunt!

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:55.940
<i>Batting second, left field, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:57.980
Oh, there's Daigo!

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:02.320
Komatsu! He's going to bunt! 
Michiru, come forward to defend!

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:04.700
<i>Th-They know...</i>

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:08.000
He's already played a bunt 
and a squeeze today.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.080
I guess they're wise to him now.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:14.410
Strike!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:19.180
<i>If she stands that far forward, bunting 
for a base hit is out of the question.</i>

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.710
<i>I have no choice but to swing.</i>

00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:28.260
<i>Maybe I can get it through 
if I roll it out to right field.</i>

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:30.890
Strike two!

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:36.220
<i>Two strikes. He's not going to bunt now.</i>

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:37.730
<i>Retake your position.</i>

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:39.300
<i>Okay.</i>

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:43.110
<i>It's no good. I can't even graze them.</i>

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:45.320
<i>I practiced so hard, but in the end,</i>

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:49.990
<i>bunting for a base hit is a sly tactic 
that won't work if they're watching for it.</i>

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:54.620
Hey! Snap out of it, Daigo!

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:57.790
Quit swinging like you're hot stuff!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:01.340
You can't do things you haven't 
practiced, John Doe #28!

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:04.100
<i>S-Sis?</i>

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:09.930
<i>Yeah. She's right!</i>

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:12.570
<i>When your back's against the wall.</i>

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:15.500
<i>stick to what you're most comfortable with!</i>

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:16.900
What?!

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:19.440
<i>A two-strike bunt?!</i>

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:01.500
Go Dolphins!

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:04.080
Tie the game, then take 
the lead and cause an upset!

00:24:04.520 --> 00:24:08.750
But now, their ace Mayumura 
Michiru is taking the mound!

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:11.920
And Touto's manager's also making a move!

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:15.430
This is the strength of the 
undisputed kings, the Touto Boys.

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:19.460
They're amazing. But I don't want to lose!

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
Ace on the Mound

00:24:20.010 --> 00:24:22.330
Next time: "Ace on the Mound!"

00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:24.700
Run to the stage of your dreams!
